  "name": "Atalaya Castle (US)",
  "scope": "Whole surviving Huntington winter house: four native building components, open north/south courtyards, central covered arched walkway and 40ft brick water tower, west entry/service wings, flat parapet roofs, 25 cowled chimneys, east recessed entry/patio, south studio skylight, projecting green iron window baskets. Exclude Brookgreen Gardens, park retail/restrooms, vegetation, animal sculpture, signs and furnishings.",
  "era": "Surviving 1931–32 masonry house, observed published 2006–07 exteriors and primary 1992 architectural description; current minor repairs and lost equipment not surveyed.",
